#               /proc/cmdline is root-only on BP31 (`cat: /proc/cmdline: Permission denied` as the adb shell user [obs gdbgfs-20261029T155047Z-steps/identity1.txt]), so it is read through the
#               Magisk `su` form of the R helper (adb exec-out su -c "CMD; r=$?; printf '\n__GP_RC=%s\n' $r"), filtered of serial|imei|mac|ssid tokens in memory (the raw line is never written).
#               su unavailable: one plain `adb shell cat` is tried; if that fails too, exactly ONE GAP naming the shell denial (cmdline-stderr.txt).
