#               Replaces golden-1/2 step 4's hand-typed adb install (blocked by agent-guard E3a).
# su-prep       TP-037 S0-3 boot 1 of the two-boot busybox delivery [research 45 "Two-boot delivery"]: lib/arm64-v8a/libbusybox.so out of the pinned Magisk-v30.7.apk (same sha pin as
#               magisk-install; extracted to a host temp file, never kept; the busybox member is pinned transitively by the APK sha pin + the zip CRC) -> `adb push` /data/local/tmp/pixos_busybox,
#               pushed sha256 checked, then (only after a match) debug.pixos.bb.done cleared, `setprop debug.pixos.bb 0` then `1` (fires the image rc's pixos_bb service, which copies it to
#               /data/magisk in the magisk domain, deletes the push and sets debug.pixos.bb.done ok|fail), one bounded 20 s on-device wait for that property. PASS iff sha matched AND done=ok.
#               Needs NO su. /data/adb is created by Magisk's own boot_complete on boot 1 (bootstages.rs:180-184), so the rc has no mkdir of it. Then reboot and run su-check (boot 2).
