# whitelisted forms: plain %x3 (length), +OFF(%x2) with OFF in 0..7 or >= 56 (decimal/hex, no :string), +OFF(%x20) (driver struct). Nothing else. Offsets: 0, 1-5 decimal digits without a leading zero, or 0x + 1-4 hex digits (r1 F7:
# `08` is an arithmetic error in bash and a registration error in the kernel; an evaluation failure is a refusal, never a pass).
wf_p21_field() { local nm=$1 fe=$2 off="" w ty; local re='^[a-z0-9_]+=\+(0x[0-9a-fA-F]{1,4}|0|[1-9][0-9]{0,4})\((%x2|%x20)\):(u8|s8|x8|u16|s16|x16|u32|s32|x32|u64|s64|x64)$'
