# Teardown state and traps (r1 F1/F5): every phone-side change a wifi mode makes is recorded in a flag; wf_cleanup (EXIT, and INT/TERM/HUP turned into an exit) undoes what is still flagged: the staged firmware copies, an active bind, armed kprobes.
# A normal run clears the flag when it has finished the step itself (a good bind and good probes stay on purpose). A signal ends in RESULT: FAIL, never PASS. SIGKILL cannot be caught (rerun wifi-fw-unbind / wifi-kprobes-off by hand).
