# wifi_mask: MAC/BSSID (bt_mask), SSID literal, PSK literal/hex of the secret file. wifi_scan_mask: first the TAIL of `cmd wifi list-scan-results` rows from the SSID column on (neighbour SSIDs are unknown literals),
# fixed columns from ScanResultUtil.dumpScanResults, android14-release framework/java/android/net/wifi/util/ScanResultUtil.java:451-: pw.printf("  %17s  %9d  %18s   %7s    %-32s  %s\n", BSSID, freq, rssiInfo, age, ssid(%1.32s), caps)
# = 2+17+2+9+2+18+3+7+4 = 64 ASCII characters before the SSID [read from source; the BP31 build may be a QPR with another format = guess, an unmatched data line is a GAP in wifi-scan]. Everything after those 64 characters is masked
